# Rich Table Widget

The `rich_table` widget renders a full-featured data table with grouping, pivot, filtering, sorting, conditional formatting, and export.

## Basic structure

```yaml
- id: my_table
  type: rich_table
  col_span: 15                          # Use >12 for wide tables with horizontal scroll
  datasource: total_by_ad              # Key from datasources (or projection key)
  # OR inline SQL (auto-creates a type: view datasource as {widget.id}__view):
  # datasource:
  #   sql: |
  #     SELECT * FROM {{source:total_by_ad}} WHERE language = 'en'
  title: My Table                       # Optional
  columns: []                           # Required. Column definitions
  column_order: [col1, col2]            # Optional. Display order
  grouping: {}                          # Optional
  pivot: {}                             # Optional
  filtering: {}                         # Optional
  sorting: {}                           # Optional
  totals: {}                            # Optional. Grand total row (enabled by default)
  selectable: true                      # Optional. Row selection (true | config object)
  highlight: {}                         # Optional. Cross-highlight from another selectable widget
  export: {}                            # Optional
  conditional_formatting: []            # Optional
  visualization: {}                     # Optional
  layout: {}                            # Optional
  data_presets: {}                      # Optional. Projection-first data presets
```

## Data presets (projection-first)

Use `data_presets` to switch between system projections of the same table source. This is for **data shape/state**, not layout.

Each preset needs `id`, `label`, and either `projection` (reference) or `sql` (inline). No "base" preset needed — the widget `datasource` is the default ("All") state.

Use `{{source:__default_view}}` in inline SQL to reference the widget's own datasource:

```yaml
- id: campaign_table
  type: rich_table
  datasource: campaign_table__default_view    # "All" state
  data_presets:
    presets:
      - id: dlo
        label: DLO
        sql: >                                # Inline SQL — filters on top of All
          SELECT * FROM {{source:__default_view}}
          WHERE lower(language) = 'dlo'
          ORDER BY costs DESC
      - id: high_roi
        label: High ROI
        description: Positive ROI campaigns   # Optional. Tooltip on hover
        projection: campaign_table__view_high_roi
        sorting:                              # Optional. Explicit sorting
          - { id: roi, desc: true }
      - id: big_spenders
        label: Big Spenders
        sql: >
          SELECT * FROM {{source:__default_view}}
          WHERE costs > 1000
```

Full config with all optional fields:

```yaml
  data_presets:
    default_preset: high_roi           # Optional. Start with this preset instead of All
    on_apply:                          # Optional. Behavior when preset is selected
      clear_user_filters: true
      clear_sorting: true
      clear_search: true
    presets:
      - id: dlo
        label: DLO
        sql: >                         # {{source:__default_view}} = widget datasource
          SELECT * FROM {{source:__default_view}} WHERE lang = 'dlo'
      - id: high_roi
        label: High ROI
        projection: view_high_roi      # Reference to named projection
```

- `{{source:__default_view}}` auto-resolves to the widget's `datasource` at load time — works even when datasource is a projection
- Inline SQL presets can reference projections directly (e.g. `{{source:table__default_view}}`) — the runtime resolves projection dependencies automatically
- UI shows `[All] [DLO] [High ROI]` — "All" is always first, active when no preset selected
- Preset bar is hidden until table data is loaded
- Clicking "All" clears active preset state (share URL no longer stores `p[widgetId]`)
- Preset apply switches widget datasource to `preset.projection` (or auto-generated key for inline `sql`)
- User filters/search/sort are still applied on top of the selected projection
- Sorting precedence: user manual sort -> preset sorting -> inferred from projection SQL `ORDER BY` -> widget default
- Share link for widget includes active preset in URL context (`ctx`)
- Smart search index automatically rebuilds when the underlying datasource changes (e.g. after preset switch)

## Columns

Three column types: `dimension`, `metric`, `calculated`.

### Dimension (grouping/category columns)

```yaml
- id: language
  label: Lang
  type: dimension
  width: { type: fixed, value: 60 }
  pinned: left                          # left | right
  mapping: { id: languages }            # Value mapping reference
  normalize: capitalize                 # capitalize | uppercase | lowercase
  overflow:
    strategy: truncate                  # truncate | wrap | expand
    tooltip: { enabled: true, maxWidth: 420 }
  hidden: false                         # Hide column
  description: "..."                    # Optional. Header tooltip text (also ai_hint fallback)
  ai_hint: "..."                        # Optional. AI context hint (string or string[])
```

### Metric (aggregated numeric columns)

```yaml
- id: costs
  label: Costs
  type: metric
  aggregate: sum                        # sum | avg | count | min | max
  format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
  description: "Total ad spend across all campaigns"
  ai_hint: "Total ad spend — use SUM for aggregation"
```

### Calculated (expression-based columns)

```yaml
- id: roi
  label: ROI
  type: calculated
  expression: "(SUM(revenue_net) - SUM(costs)) / NULLIF(SUM(costs), 0) * 100"
  format: { type: percent, decimals: 0, suffix: "%" }
```

### Column format

```yaml
format:
  type: number | currency | percent
  decimals: 2                           # Optional
  prefix: "$"                           # Optional
  suffix: "%"                           # Optional
  locale: "en-US"                       # Optional. BCP 47 locale tag (default: en-US)
  abbreviate_above: 1000                # Optional. Min abs(value) to abbreviate (requires abbreviate_numbers)
```

### Column width

```yaml
# Simple fixed width
width: 120

# Detailed config
width:
  type: fixed | flex | auto
  value: 120                            # For fixed: pixels. For flex: weight
  min: 80                               # Optional. Min width in px
  max: 400                              # Optional. Max width in px
```

### Column header tooltips

Three levels of column header tooltips, each building on the previous:

**Level 1 — Auto (truncation):** When the header label is truncated (ellipsis), hovering shows the full label. No config needed — always active.

**Level 2 — Description:** Static text shown on hover, regardless of truncation. Also serves as `ai_hint` fallback when no explicit `ai_hint` is set.

```yaml
- id: ecpa
  label: eCPA
  type: calculated
  expression: "SUM(costs) / NULLIF(SUM(action), 0)"
  description: >-
    Effective Cost Per Action.
    Formula: SUM(costs) / NULLIF(SUM(action), 0)
```

**Level 3 — Programmable (SQL + template):** A template with a `context` block populated via DuckDB SQL on hover. `{{_self}}` resolves to the current active datasource (respects data presets).

```yaml
- id: roi
  label: ROI
  type: calculated
  description: Return on Investment
  tooltip:
    context:
      sql: |
        SELECT
          ROUND(AVG(roi_val), 1) as avg_roi,
          COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE roi_val > 0) as profitable,
          COUNT(*) as total
        FROM {{_self}}
    template: |
      **{{column.label}}**
      {{column.description}}
      ---
      Avg: {{context.avg_roi}}%
      Profitable: {{context.profitable}}/{{context.total}}
```

Template variables: `{{column.id}}`, `{{column.label}}`, `{{column.description}}`, `{{context.*}}`.

## Grouping

```yaml
grouping:
  enabled: true
  levels: [language, media_source, campaign]   # Column ids for group hierarchy
  subtotal_levels: [[language, media_source]]  # Show subtotals at these levels
  default_expanded: false                      # Start collapsed
  sticky:
    active_group_headers: true                 # Sticky group headers on scroll
    subtotals_under_grand: true                # Subtotals visible under grand total
```

## Pivot

Pivot transforms rows into a cross-tabulation:

```yaml
pivot:
  rows:
    - id: plan_name
      label: Type
    - id: payment_source
      label: Payment source
  columns:
    - id: day
      label: Day
      type: date                         # date | string | number
      desc: true                          # pivot values sort direction
  values:
    - id: revenue_net
      label: Revenue
      aggregate: sum                     # sum | avg | count | min | max
      format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
  totals:
    row: true                            # Show row totals
    column: true                         # Show column totals
  grand_total_label: "Total"             # Optional
```

When using pivot, also define `columns` for the static row dimensions and a `grand_total` metric column:

```yaml
columns:
  - id: plan_name
    label: Type
    type: dimension
    pinned: left
  - id: payment_source
    label: Payment source
    type: dimension
    pinned: left
  - id: grand_total
    label: Total
    type: metric
    aggregate: sum
    format: { type: currency, decimals: 0 }
  # Dynamic pivot columns are injected automatically
```

## Filtering (column-level)

```yaml
filtering:
  enabled: true
  show_filter_row: true                  # Show inline filter row under header
  global_search: true                    # Enable smart search (shorthand)
  columns:
    - { id: language, type: select, multi: true }
    - { id: media_source, type: select }
    - { id: campaign, type: text, match: contains }   # contains | starts_with | ends_with
    - { id: costs, type: number, operator: ">" }       # > | < | >= | <= | = | between
    - { id: install_date, type: date, operator: between }
```

### Smart Table Search (`global_search`)

Enable with `global_search: true` (or expanded form below). The search input appears in the table header and supports natural queries like `en fb cost>300 not nogti`.

```yaml
filtering:
  global_search: true                    # Shorthand: enable with defaults

  # Expanded form:
  global_search:
    enabled: true
    show_token_pills: false              # Show parsed-tokens badge (default: false, overridable via DevTools)
    token_pills_expanded: true           # Start pills tray expanded (default: true)
```

**Token types recognized:**

| Token | Example | Resolves to |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| Keyword | `en` | Filter on matching dimension value (Orama FTS) |
| Quoted phrase | `"hello world"` | Text search `ILIKE '%hello world%'` |
| Negation | `not nogti`, `-nogti`, `!nogti` | Exclusion `NOT ILIKE '%nogti%'` |
| Range | `costs>300`, `ecpa<=50` | Column filter with operator |
| Spaced range | `costs > 300` | Auto-normalized to `costs>300` |

**How it works:**

1. On focus, an Orama FTS index is built from DuckDB dimension values (UNION ALL batch query)
2. Values are ranked by a composite priority: metric-rank (from sort metrics), row frequency, sort position, column order
3. Fuzzy column matching (Levenshtein) resolves typos in range expressions (`cost>300` → `costs>300`)
4. Resolved tokens are compiled to SQL WHERE clauses and injected as inline column filters (highlighted in blue)
5. Results re-ranked by combining Orama text score with value priority

**DevTools integration:**

- `Cmd+Shift+D` / `Ctrl+Shift+D` opens DevTools (works in production)
- **Search tab**: build indexes, inspect field weights, test queries with raw Orama hits and resolved tokens

## Sorting

```yaml
sorting:
  enabled: true
  multi: true                            # Allow multi-column sort
  default:                               # Optional. Initial sort order
    - { id: costs, desc: true }
```

## Totals

Grand total row is shown by default when there are metric columns. Controls:

```yaml
totals:
  enabled: true                          # Default: true (show grand total row)
  sticky: bottom                         # true (sticky top) | 'bottom' (sticky bottom, default) | false
  label: "Total"                         # Optional. Label for grand total row
```

- Totals are always computed with `SUM` by default; uses the column's `aggregate` if specified.
- Works with both flat (ungrouped) and grouped tables.
- Set `enabled: false` to hide the grand total row entirely.
- Legacy: `grouping.sticky.grand_total` is still supported as fallback.

## Selectable rows

Enable row selection with `selectable`. The full Arrow row is stored in a global selection store and can be consumed by other widgets via `${selection.*}` SQL templates or Handlebars `{{selection.*}}`.

```yaml
# Simple: single-select, click to highlight
selectable: true

# Multi-select with checkboxes and select-all
selectable:
  multi: true
  select_all: true

# When consumers reference columns not in widget.columns (e.g. ${selection.X('experiment_id')})
selectable:
  columns: [id, name, experiment_id]
```

Identity uses the Arrow row index (`_arrowIndex`). By default, dimension columns are stored. Use `selectable.columns` when consumer projections reference columns not in `widget.columns` — the system also auto-computes required columns from `${selection.widget_id("col")}` references in projection SQL. Selection is cleared automatically when data re-fetches.

A widget with `selectable` cannot also have `highlight` (mutually exclusive).

### Cross-highlight

Consumer tables can visually highlight rows matching another widget's selection. Values are extracted from the stored full rows by the specified `column`:

```yaml
highlight:
  selection: campaigns_table           # Source widget id
  column: campaign_id                  # Column to match (in both source rows and this table)

# Multiple sources
highlight:
  - selection: campaigns_table
    column: campaign_id
  - selection: countries_table
    column: country_code
```

### Selection templates in projections

Consumer widgets reference selections in projection SQL. Column is always specified explicitly:

```yaml
projections:
  filtered_by_selection:
    sql: |
      SELECT * FROM {{source:main}}
      WHERE 1=1 ${selection.campaigns_table('campaign_id')}
```

| Template | Selected | Empty |
|---|---|---|
| `${selection.widget('col')}` | `AND col IN ('a','b')` | `AND 1=1` |
| `${selection.widget('col').if_set}` | `AND col IN (...)` | `` (empty) |
| `${selection.widget('col').value}` | `'first_val'` | `NULL` |
| `${selection.widget('col').values}` | `'a', 'b'` | `` (empty) |

## Export

CSV download from the kebab menu (⋮) in the table header. Enabled by default for all tables — no config needed. Use `export` to customize or disable.

```yaml
# Disable export
export:
  enabled: false

# Customize (all fields optional — shown with defaults)
export:
  enabled: true                          # Default: true (opt-out with false)
  formats: [csv]                         # Supported: csv (excel planned)
  include_group_rows: false              # Include group header rows in CSV
  include_subtotals: false               # Include subtotal rows in CSV
```

Exports all rows matching current filters and sorting — not just the visible viewport.

## Conditional formatting

### Color scale

```yaml
conditional_formatting:
  - column: roi
    type: color_scale
    palette: red_white_green             # red_white_green | red_yellow_green
    apply_to: cell                       # cell | text
    value_sql: |
      CASE
        WHEN costs > 2000 AND roi < 0 THEN -100
        WHEN roi >= 60 THEN 100
        ELSE roi
      END
    steps:
      - { value: -100, color: "#f3b3b3" }
      - { value: 0, color: "#f7f7f7" }
      - { value: 60, color: "#9cc3b0" }
```

- `value_sql` is optional and supported for `color_scale` rules.
- It is evaluated in table SQL and used as the color-scale input value for `data` rows.
- If `value_sql` is not set (or returns non-numeric), the widget falls back to the raw column value.

### Icon set

```yaml
  - column: status
    type: icon_set
    rules:
      - { op: ">=", value: 80, icon: CheckCircle }
      - { op: ">=", value: 50, icon: AlertTriangle }
      - { op: "<", value: 50, icon: XCircle }
```

### Data bar

```yaml
  - column: costs
    type: data_bar
    min: 0
    max: 10000
    color: "#3b82f6"
```

## Visualization

```yaml
visualization:
  density: compact | comfortable | spacious
  row_height: small | medium | large | xlarge | 2xlarge
  zebra: true
  zebra_rows: even | odd
  style: default | minimal | structured | bloomberg | vercel
  style_switcher: true                   # Show style toggle in UI
  abbreviate_numbers:                    # Optional. Abbreviate large numbers
    enabled: true                        # Shorthand: all row types
```

### Abbreviate numbers

Abbreviates numeric values using compact notation (1000 → $1K, 1500000 → $1.5M). Disabled by default. Configured inside `visualization`.

```yaml
# Enable for all row types
visualization:
  abbreviate_numbers:
    enabled: true

# Granular: per row type
visualization:
  abbreviate_numbers:
    rows: true                          # Data rows
    subtotals: true                     # Subtotal rows
    totals: false                       # Grand total row
```

- `enabled: true` is shorthand for `{ rows: true, subtotals: true, totals: true }`
- Applies only to numeric columns (`metric`, `calculated`)
- Full value is shown on hover (tooltip)
- Uses `Intl.NumberFormat` with `notation: 'compact'` (K, M, B suffixes)
- Respects `locale` from column `format` (default: `en-US`)
- Per-column `abbreviate_above` threshold — values with `abs(value) < threshold` stay fully formatted

## Actions with skill reference

Actions can trigger write skills via the `skill` field:

```yaml
actions:
  pause:
    label: Pause Campaign
    icon: pause
    quick: true
    when: "effective_status = 'ACTIVE'"
    skill: pause_campaign           # Datasource key for write skill

  archive:
    label: Archive Campaign
    icon: archive
    destructive: true               # Shows "Are you sure?" dialog first
    skill: archive_campaign
```

- `skill` — references a write skill datasource key (UPDATE/INSERT SQL)
- `destructive: true` — client-side confirmation dialog before executing
- When row is mutating (shimmer ON), all actions are disabled

## Editable columns with skill reference

Editable columns can trigger write skills on save:

```yaml
- id: daily_budget
  label: Daily Budget
  type: metric
  aggregate: sum
  format: { type: currency, decimals: 2 }
  editable: true
  skill: update_campaign_budget     # Write skill executed on save
```

When `skill` is set, the edit save triggers `useSkillWrite.execute()` instead of just logging.

## Row shimmer during mutation

When a write skill is executing, the affected row shows a pulse animation (`animate-pulse opacity-70`). During this state:
- All action buttons are disabled
- Editable cells are read-only
- The row is visually dimmed to indicate "in progress"

## Layout presets & responsive

```yaml
layout:
  default_preset: comfortable
  show_reset: false
  presets:
    - id: compact
      label: Compact
      density: compact
      row_height: small
      columns:
        - id: campaign
          width: { type: flex, value: 2, min: 180, max: 420 }
        - id: costs
          width: { type: fixed, value: 110 }
    - id: comfortable
      label: Comfortable
      density: comfortable
      row_height: large
      columns:
        - id: campaign
          width: { type: flex, value: 3, min: 220, max: 520 }
  responsive:
    - max_width: 1024
      preset: compact                    # Switch preset on smaller screens
```
